{# style — re-skins its subtree's design tokens (accent/neutral) and wraps a child
   block list (style-block spec §4.4). Follows the global color mode: the scoped <style>
   carries both light and dark var sets, switched by data-theme — variables only, one of
   the enumerated inline emitters (visual builder spec §2.5). Spacing and shadow are
   settings on the `root` target; the custom-CSS class hook is the Advanced tab's CSS
   classes, emitted by style_classes(). 'inherit'/absent/unknown accent|neutral = don't
   apply that override.
   NOTE (canvas): the <style> is rendered LAST, AFTER __inner, so the canvas bridge's
   host (w.firstElementChild) is always the content wrapper — never the <style> (P1). #}
{% set scope = theme_style_scope(data.accent|default(''), data.neutral|default('')) %}
<div class="thallo-block thallo-block-style{{ scope.class }}{{ style_classes('root') }}"{{ style_attrs('root') }}>
  <div class="thallo-block-style__inner"{{ slot_attrs('content') }}>{{ blocks(data.content|default([])) }}</div>
  {{ scope.style }}
</div>
